---
// Landing page — the Wollack Systems story, cut to the Dale test (Oct 5): why
// it can't wait, how it works at your plant, and the work. The origin and the
// founder live on /about, which owns them. Canonical slate + electric blue
// Industrial Editorial theme (see DESIGN.md).
// Product detail lives on /journeyman (the "Rust & Iron" variant page).
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  organization,
  personWillWollack,
  personEthanDavidson,
  webSite,
} from '@/lib/schema';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Wollack Systems: capturing manufacturing expertise before it retires"
  description="Wollack Systems writes down what America's best machinists know, hands-free, before it retires with them. A mic on the operator, and your plant gets the written record."
  path="/"
  jsonLd={[organization(), personWillWollack(), personEthanDavidson(), webSite()]}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Knowledge capture for American manufacturing</p>
        <h1>American manufacturing is about to forget how it works. We're here to write it down.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Somewhere right now, a plant is calling back an operator who retired six years ago. Ear
          to the housing, one tap with a small hammer.
          {" "}<strong>The machine runs.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="lede-strong">
          That invoice is why Wollack Systems exists. We write down what your best people know,
          before it retires with them.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:willwollack@gmail.com?subject=Walkthrough%20request"
            >Book a walkthrough</a
          >
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/about/">Meet the founder</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="invoice-card" aria-label="The famous itemized invoice">
        <div class="invoice-head">INVOICE</div>
        <table>
          <caption class="sr-only">Itemized repair invoice</caption>
          <tr><td>Repair to machine</td><td class="num">$10,000</td></tr>
          <tr class="invoice-divider"><td colspan="2">Itemized, as requested:</td></tr>
          <tr><td>One hammer</td><td class="num">$5</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Knowing where to tap</td><td class="num">$9,995</td></tr>
          <tr class="invoice-total"><td>TOTAL</td><td class="num">$10,000</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="invoice-note">$9,995 was knowledge. Nobody wrote it down. We do.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- The mission -->
  <section class="section" id="mission">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why it can't wait.</h2>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact-number">1 in 4</div>
          <p>
            of US manufacturing workers are 55 or older, per the
            {" "}<a class="inline-link" href="https://www.bls.gov/cps/cpsaat18b.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BLS Current Population Survey</a>.
            They're leaving together.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="fact-number">First time</div>
          <p>AI can finally learn from a recording. It can't go get one. That's our job.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="section-close">
        When the best troubleshooter on the floor retires, the line slows down and nobody can say
        why. They're still reachable. Not for long.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The mechanism: what a Dale asks after "why now" — what happens at MY
       plant. Three steps, same markup as before; the origin that used to
       live here moved to /about, which owns it. -->
  <section class="section section-tinted" id="how">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How it works at your plant.</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>A mic on the operator.</h3>
          <p>
            We clip on a microphone and a small camera. The operator does the job and explains it
            out loud, in their own words.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Talk becomes the written record.</h3>
          <p>
            Every session comes back in writing: step by step, searchable, in the operator's own
            words. Your plant owns the recordings.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Your team asks the library.</h3>
          <p>
            A new hire, the midnight shift, anyone. Ask a plain question and get the answer, with
            the segment it came from.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The work -->
  <section class="section" id="work">
    <div class="container pricing-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The work</p>
      <p class="price-anchor"><strong>Journeyman</strong></p>
      <p class="price-sub">
        Journeyman turns the written record into a library your team can ask questions of.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row cta-center">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/journeyman/">See how Journeyman works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="section section-paper" id="book">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>The people who know how to run your plant<br />are retiring right now.</h2>
      <p class="section-close-ink">
        One conversation tells you what capture would look like on your floor.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row cta-center">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:willwollack@gmail.com?subject=Walkthrough%20request"
          >Book a walkthrough</a
        >
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://etok.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >Meet the cofounder</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Page-scoped: inline text links inside step copy on the dark ground. */
  .inline-link {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-accent-blue);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .inline-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-blue);
  }
</style>
